 to 43.0%26#37;), non-Hispanic white (39.6%26#37; to 46.5%26#37;), non-Hispanic black (41.2%26#37; to 44.9%26#37;), and non-Hispanic Asian (41.5%26#37; to 49.6%26#37;) adults. In 2011, there was no statistically significant difference among the four groups examined, but in 2016, Hispanic adults were less likely than non-Hispanic white and non- Hispanic Asian adults to have had a fasting test, and non-Hispanic Asian adults were more likely than non-Hispanic black adults to have had one.","hasAlt":true,"isDecorative":false,"isMissingAlt":false,"ariaHidden":false,"rolePresentation":false,"renderedWidth":739,"renderedHeight":506,"naturalWidth":739,"naturalHeight":506,"loading":null,"decoding":"async","altVerdict":"TOO_LONG","altReason":"alt text is 833 characters — consider a caption or description","bytes":31416},{"src":"https://www.cdc.gov/TemplatePackage/5.0/img/logo/cdc-logo-tag-right.svg","alt":"Centers for Disease Control and Prevention","hasAlt":true,"isDecorative":false,"isMissingAlt":false,"ariaHidden":false,"rolePresentation":false,"renderedWidth":283,"renderedHeight":66,"naturalWidth":827,"naturalHeight":193,"loading":null,"decoding":null,"altVerdict":"GOOD","altReason":"present, no red flags","bytes":4780},{"src":"https://www.cdc.gov/TemplatePackage/contrib/libs/cdc/c2r/crlogo.svg","alt":"Content Credentials logo","hasAlt":true,"isDecorative":false,"isMissingAlt":false,"ariaHidden":false,"rolePresentation":false,"renderedWidth":25,"renderedHeight":150,"naturalWidth":150,"naturalHeight":150,"loading":null,"decoding":null,"altVerdict":"GOOD","altReason":"present, no red flags","bytes":1490}]}}